Fix a bug in two files. Work in `/Users/felix/code/.claude/worktrees/beijian+spare-parts-management/beijian/`

### Fix 1: `src/components/category-form-dialog.tsx` — handleSave swallows errors

Find the `handleSave` function. It does `fetch()` but doesn't check `res.ok`. Errors are silently swallowed. Fix it to check `res.ok` and show an alert on failure, only closing the dialog on success:

```typescript
const handleSave = async () => {
    if (!name.trim()) return;
    setSaving(true);
    try {
      const method = category ? "PUT" : "POST";
      const url = category
        ? `/api/categories/${category.id}`
        : "/api/categories";
      const res = await fetch(url, {
        method,
        headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
        body: JSON.stringify({ name: name.trim(), parentId: parentId || null, description }),
      });
      if (!res.ok) {
        const err = await res.json();
        alert(err.error || "保存失败");
        return;
      }
      onOpenChange(false);
      onSaved();
    } catch {
      alert("网络错误，保存失败");
    } finally {
      setSaving(false);
    }
};
```

### Fix 2: `src/app/categories/page.tsx` — load() has no error handling

Wrap load() in try/catch:

```typescript
const load = async () => {
    try {
      const res = await fetch("/api/categories");
      const data = await res.json();
      setCategories(data);
    } catch {
      // silently handle — will show empty state
    }
};
```

### After fixes

Run `npm run build` to verify it compiles.

Commit:
```bash
git add -A
git commit -m "fix: add error handling to category dialog and page

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>"
```

Report when done.

